158:**2c. Samples (`get_sample_files`, both phases)** *(finding 7; rev 3 ? new-10)*: phase 1 ? files
159:with `FileType.VideoExtensions` = `.mp4 .m4v .avi .mkv .wmv .vob .m2ts .ts .mpeg .mpg .m2v .m2p`
160:whose path contains `sample` (case-insensitive), or where the literal `sample[:-4] + ".sfv"`
161:sibling exists (pyrescene's exact slice ? for extensions ﾐ岱・3 chars, e.g. `.m2ts`/`.mpeg`, this
162:tests a quirky name; the quirk is preserved and tested); phase 2 ? remaining videos whose
163:**basename appears case-sensitively in any SFV's entries** anywhere in the release.
164:
165:**2d. Stored files (`generate_srr` consumption + `get_proof_files` chain, exact port)**
166:*(findings 8, 9; rev 3 ? new-1, new-6)*: `*.nfo` with pyrescene's filtering (skip `imdb.nfo`,
167:`tvmaze.nfo`; `no.nfo` per the excerpt's condition); `*.m3u`; `*.log` with pyrescene's log filter;
168:`*.cue`; pre-existing `*.srs` files ? with the excerpt's precedence: a freshly GENERATED SRS for
169:the same relative path supersedes a pre-existing one (single stored entry, no collision error);
170:the conditional fix RAR the excerpt stores. NON-keyword
171:images = ALL images outside keyword paths (not just root-level) run `always_skip` (exact
172:predicates: space in basename, stem ending `folder`, basename containing `albumartsmall`,
173:basename starting `albumart_{`) then `store_rls_root` (basename starting `00`/`01`/`001` ﾐ岱ｸ
174:accept; else size **> 100000 bytes exactly** AND similar-named to nfo/sfv/rars AND not a
175:fixed-resolution cover ﾐ岱ｸ accept; else skip + warning). Keyword-path images (path contains
176:`proof`/`sample`/`cover`/`screenshots`/`compare`) are accepted **before** `always_skip` runs.
177:The `more_images` CLI option is not exposed; its default-off behavior is what is ported.
178:Independent pass `filter_proof_rar_files`: ANY `*.rar` under the root with `proof` in its path
179:whose packed blocks include an image ﾐ岱ｸ stored. `strip_zeros`/`similar_to_good_name`/
180:`fixed_resolution_cover` ported per the excerpt (including M3U-similarity).
181:
182:**2e. First-RAR handling** *(finding 12, rev 3)*: pyrescene's `get_start_rar_files` derives
183:`main_rars` ONLY from the selected SFVs' entries ? it never discovers loose RAR sets, and an SFV
184:listing multiple chains contributes EVERY first RAR it references (one set input may carry
185:multiple chains; the writer handles each chain ? new-7, with test). Loose-RAR-folder discovery is
186:therefore **[DIVERGENCE: extension]**, active only when zero SFVs exist anywhere under the root:
187:first-volume RARs found outside dirs excluded by 2a rules 3-6 become `MainSets` entries. Sets
188:found via SFV subsume their volumes (no double-discovery).
189:
190:**Ordering** *(finding 13, rev 4)*: pyrescene's byte order is RAW `os.walk` enumeration ?
191:filesystem-dependent and not reproducible in general. **[DIVERGENCE: determinism]** we order every
192:collection by top-down traversal with ORDINAL case-sensitive sorting of directory and file names
193:at each level, applied per category pass in pyrescene's `generate_srr` sequence (nfo ﾐ岱ｸ m3u ﾐ岱ｸ
194:proof ﾐ岱ｸ log ﾐ岱ｸ cue ﾐ岱ｸ srs ﾐ岱ｸ sfvs/sets). Excluded-SFV order has NO parity target at all: the
195:excerpt's `get_unwanted_sfvs` is `list(set(allsfvs) - set(wantedsfvs))` ? a hash-dependent set
196:difference, nondeterministic even across pyrescene runs ? so our canonical traversal order for
197:`SubtitleSfvs` is definitionally a **[DIVERGENCE: determinism]**, and each golden-fixture tree
198:contains at most ONE excluded SFV so nested-SRR ordering can never differ from pyrescene's. On NTFS ? where the
199:golden fixtures are generated ? directory enumeration is name-ordered, so the golden comparison
200:holds in practice; on other filesystems pyrescene itself is nondeterministic and our order is the
201:documented canonical one. UI may *display* `DetectedSets` natural-sorted; creation consumes
202:traversal order. `Warnings` sort by concerned path (ordinal).
203:
204:**Error contract** *(finding 14; rev 4)*: **[DIVERGENCE: hardening]** scanner I/O failures are
205:per-item warnings (item classified stored-only when readable metadata suffices, otherwise
206:skipped) ? the excerpt catches only selected exceptions (`TypeError` in walking, `ValueError` in
207:RAR reading) and would crash on the rest; we degrade gracefully and say so per item. Enumeration
208:failure of the root itself ﾐ岱ｸ error result via a `Warnings`-only result with empty collections. The scanner takes a
209:`CancellationToken` and throws `OperationCanceledException` promptly.
