211:## 3. App.Core ? CreatorViewModel
212:
213:- `InputPath` accepts a directory (`Directory.Exists`). New `BrowseInputFolderCommand`
214:  (`IFileDialogService.OpenFolderAsync`).
215:- **Scan lifecycle** *(finding 14)*: each directory input bumps a scan generation (the
216:  `InspectorViewModel._loadGeneration` house pattern), cancels the previous scan's CTS, runs
217:  `Scan` in `Task.Run`, and applies results on the UI thread ONLY if its generation is still
218:  current. `IsScanning` gates Create and re-input. Stale scans can never overwrite newer state.
219:- On results: populate `DetectedSets` (new read-only collection), `StoredFiles` (path-prefixed
220:  logical names), `ExtraSampleFiles`, `ExtraSubtitleSfvFiles`; status summary
221:  `"2 RAR sets ﾐ薦 1 sample ﾐ薦 4 stored files"` + warnings; music-only ﾐ岱ｸ error status, Create
222:  disabled for folder mode.
223:- **Output path** *(finding 15)*: the VM tracks whether `OutputPath` is auto-generated or
224:  user-edited (auto-generated values are replaced on re-scan; user edits are never clobbered ?
225:  refines the existing blank-only convention). Default: `<releaseRoot parent>/<releaseRootName>.srr`
226:  built with `Path.Combine` on the normalized root (trailing separators trimmed; filesystem roots
227:  like `D:\` produce an error status instead of a name).
228:- **Generated artifacts** *(findings 10, 11; rev 3 ? new-3)*: SRS and nested-SRR outputs are
229:  produced in a TEMP working directory mirroring the root-relative layout (pyrescene's model) and
230:  handed to the writer as explicit `StoredFileEntry` (source in temp, logical name root-relative ?
231:  permitted by ﾐ岱ｨ1a). Collision keying matches the excerpt exactly: by full relative STEM (same
232:  stem in *different* directories is NOT a collision); only same-stem collisions keep the full
233:  source extension (`x.mkv.srs`). One subtitle SFV may yield MULTIPLE nested SRRs (per the
234:  excerpt's `create_srr_for_subs` returning a list). Excerpt edge behaviors ported: an
235:  SRS-creation failure stores the failure `.txt` pyrescene writes; a RAR-backed `.vob` sample
236:  produces a nested SRR. Cancellation deletes the temp working dir; artifacts never overwrite
237:  user files (temp dir is exclusive per scan generation).
238:- Creation (folder mode): `CreateFromInputsAsync(outputPath, DetectedSets paths in order,
239:  releaseRoot, storeRelativePaths: true, storedFiles, options, ct)`. File mode: unchanged.
240:- `ISRRCreationService`/`SRRCreationService` gain the pass-through.
241:
242:## 4. UI (ReScene.Manager)
243:
244:Both surfaces (Advanced `CreatorView.axaml`, wizard `CreateSRRWizardBody.axaml` step "1 of 5"):
245:
246:- "Browse folderﾐ祖" beside "Browse"; the typeable box accepts either path kind.
247:- Read-only `DetectedSets` list (ItemsControl of `RelativeName`) under the input row, visible when
248:  a folder scan found sets; `FieldStatusLine` carries the summary/warnings; a busy indicator while
249:  `IsScanning`.
250:- Wizard: the samples/subs step ("Step 2 of 5") and stored-files step ("Step 3 of 5") show the
251:  pre-populated lists; all existing add/remove/reorder controls keep working. Manual edits persist
252:  until the input changes (re-scan replaces collections).
253:
254:### 4a. Accessibility contract (from the codex accessibility addendum, proportionate scope)
255:
256:- **Naming:** the two browse buttons get distinct `AutomationProperties.Name` values ("Browse
257:  input file", "Browse release folder"); the input box gets a `HelpText` stating it accepts a
258:  file or release-folder path; the `DetectedSets` ItemsControl and each pre-populated list get
259:  automation names including counts ("Detected RAR sets, 2 items").
260:- **Status announcements:** scan start/finish/warnings/errors flow through the existing
261:  `FieldStatusLine`/status text (already the app's live-status pattern); stale-generation results
262:  are discarded before reaching it, so no stale announcements. Create-disabled reasons appear in
263:  the same status text, not only as a disabled button.
264:- **Keyboard & focus:** the path box is never disabled while focused (scan gating disables
265:  Create, not the editor); focus returns to the invoking browse button after the native picker
266:  closes; tab order is input box ﾐ岱ｸ browse file ﾐ岱ｸ browse folder ﾐ岱ｸ detected list ﾐ岱ｸ onward.
267:- **Detected-sets list:** bounded height with vertical scrolling (never grows the window).
268:- **Verification (Spec 1 scope):** automation names/help text asserted via the agent bridge
269:  (`ava_props` on the live controls) and unit-level peer checks; full NVDA/Narrator/high-DPI/
270:  contrast-theme lab passes are explicitly out of scope for Spec 1 and tracked as a follow-up.
271:
272:## 5. Error handling
273:
274:| Case | Behavior |
275:|---|---|
276:| Zero main sets, storable files exist (fix release) | Storage-only SRR (ﾐ岱ｨ1 zero-input mode) + warning. |
277:| Nothing storable at all | Header-only SRR (pyrescene parity ? its header-only creation path); warning status. |
278:| Music-only release | Error status naming Spec 2; Create disabled (folder mode). Mixed ﾐ岱ｸ ﾐ岱ｨ2b. |
279:| SFV references a missing volume | Error result naming the file; no partial output; existing destination preserved. |
280:| Non-first-volume `.rar` input | Error result (pyrescene `ValueError` parity). |
281:| Source outside root / SFV entry escaping its directory / logical-name collision | Error result naming the offender (ﾐ岱ｨ1a). |
282:| Output path equals an input/source | Error result (ﾐ岱ｨ1). |
283:| Scanner per-item I/O errors | Warning; scan continues (ﾐ岱ｨ2 error contract). |
284:| Unreadable/RAR5 proof RAR | Warning; SFV excluded from sets (proof), per ﾐ岱ｨ2a rule 4. |
285:| Scan superseded by newer input | Silently discarded (generation guard, ﾐ岱ｨ3). |
286:
287:## 6. Testing
288:
289:**Golden fixtures (non-circular oracle)** *(finding 16; rev 3 ? new-8)*: a committed generator
290:script (`ReScene.Lib/ReScene.Tests/TestData/multiset/generate-golden.py` + README) builds
291:synthetic release trees (2-disc RAR sets via SRRTestDataBuilder-equivalent store-mode RARs + real
292:SFVs + nfo + Sample/ + Subs/ + junk files) and runs the **local pyrescene** over them. The README
293:records the pyrescene git commit hash, Python version, exact command line, and options used;
294:regeneration asserts the checkout matches that hash. "App-name normalized" is defined: before
295:byte comparison, each SRR's header-block app-name field (and only it) is replaced by the fixed
296:string `NORMALIZED`, via an independent minimal block-splitter in the test (documented offsets,
297:not the production parser). The resulting `.srr` files are committed as golden fixtures. Lib tests assert OUR `CreateFromInputsAsync` output is **byte-identical** to
298:the golden SRR for the same tree (app-name field normalized), which proves separators, stored
299:names, volume names, and block order in one stroke. The existing pyrescene 2-CD fixture stays as
300:a read-side regression anchor.
301:
302:**Lib:** golden byte-equality (above); zero-input storage-only SRR; zero-input zero-file
303:rejection; single-SFV and single-RAR delegation byte-identical to pre-change output (existing
304:tests untouched); missing volume / non-first RAR / outside-root / SFV-escape / name-collision /
305:output-equals-input error paths; cancellation and failure leave a pre-seeded destination intact;
306:temp file cleaned up.
307:
308:**Scanner:** one test per decision-tree branch and per finding: subpack release keeps vobsub SFVs;
309:`pass`-fallthrough (subs-named SFV under a `cover` dir is still excluded); exact-set vs substring
310:pardir rules; proof single-entry/lowercase-`.rar`/last-block-wins/RAR5/missing-RAR variants; `Subs/CD1`;
311:rescue fallback (multi-entry re-admission; music ﾐ岱ｸ `MusicSfvs`); mixed release policy; both sample
312:phases (incl. differently-located SFV reference); `always_skip` exact predicates + keyword-dir
313:bypass (`Proof/Folder.jpg` stored, root `Folder.jpg` skipped, `MyFolder.png` skipped,
314:`AlbumArtLarge` NOT skipped, `AlbumArt_{...}` skipped); `store_rls_root` 00/01-prefix + size +
315:similar-name + resolution branches (exact 100000-byte boundary; M3U-only similarity);
316:non-singleton and no-packed-block proof SFVs; independent proof-RAR pass; multi-chain SFV (all
317:first RARs retained); loose-RAR divergence gating; traversal ordering incl. case-only names;
318:`sample[:-4]` quirk extensions; nfo filtering (`imdb.nfo`/`tvmaze.nfo`); m3u/log/cue/srs storage;
319:subpack main-SFV nested processing; per-item I/O warning; cancellation (incl. temp-artifact
320:cleanup).
321:
322:**VM:** stub-scanner population; generation guard (reverse completion order ? old scan result
323:discarded); `IsScanning` gates; auto vs user-edited output path across re-scans; music-only
324:disables Create; creation captures ordered multi-input call; artifact collision skip+warning.
325:
326:**E2E (agent bridge):** drive both surfaces on a synthesized two-disc release folder; verify
327:detected-sets readout, pre-populated wizard steps, created SRR opens in the Inspector with both
328:sets and in the Reconstructor with both discs in the Set column.
329:
330:**Review gates:** codex reviews this spec (done ? rev 2 addresses its 16 findings), the
331:implementation plan, and every implementation task's diff.
332:
